openwrt-patches: drop the QSDK busybox config override

The QSDK openwrt-patches tree ships a busybox extension whose
Package/busybox/overrideconfig makes the scan source its own Config.in,
which in turn sources Config-defaults.in (ARPING/TIMEOUT default y,
FEATURE_EDITING_MAX_LEN 1024). In the audited tree that override never
took effect: tmp/info/.packageinfo-busybox was stale, so the Kconfig
metadata came only from feeds/base/utils/busybox/Config.in, and the
audited firmware was built with CONFIG_BUSYBOX_CUSTOM=n and the OpenWrt
applet defaults (build_dir/busybox .../.config: EDITING_MAX_LEN=512, no
CONFIG_TIMEOUT, 261 =y entries).

A fresh scan on CI does pick the override up and flips 39
CONFIG_BUSYBOX_DEFAULT_* plus TIMEOUT/EDITING_MAX_LEN, i.e. the gate
would silently produce a different busybox than the audited one. Keep the
install extension (inetd/inittab/rcS, which the audited build did apply)
and the patches/, drop only the config override, so the CI build matches
the audited firmware. Registered in build/known-delta.conf.

Apply from the buildroot top:  patch -p1 < 0017-...

--- a/openwrt-patches/package/utils/busybox/busybox.mk
+++ b/openwrt-patches/package/utils/busybox/busybox.mk
@@ -19,4 +19,5 @@
 endef
 
 Package/busybox/install += $(newline)$(busybox_install_append)
-Package/busybox/overrideconfig = $(newline)$(busybox_config_append)
+# 24.10-6.6：去掉 QSDK 的 busybox 配置覆盖（原因见 build/build-fixes/SERIES 0017）
+# Package/busybox/overrideconfig = $(newline)$(busybox_config_append)
